{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong","id":854749,"title":"Aren't the changing breeds doing breeding all wrong?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-28T17:39:55-07:00","id":854749,"title":"Aren't the changing breeds doing breeding all wrong?","content":"So the garou are loosing lots of numbers, and the wolf population is low. The apocalypse is coming, the black spirals breed metis after metis for their front line infantry... Isn't this wrong? No, I don't mean 'wrong' as in 'oh no, world of darkness, you're being so horrible' I mean &quot;this isn't really the logical method&quot;<br /> <br /> Now this is more more or less true for changing breeds, because the pregnancy ranges from ten babies per week to one in a thousand years and all the parents will die, and maybe this is just my weaver tainted mind looking for effeciency where it would offend, but my argument: The animal breed should be the most populous.<br /> <br /> Let's assume it takes a year or two to train cubs.<br /> <br /> You make one human every nine months<br /> OR<br /> One metis every six months<br /> OR<br /> You make aproximately six lupus (As much as 12) over three months, but can only do this once a year.<br /> <br /> Humans will take... let's assume they change at 14.<br /> Metis take about 8<br /> Lupus take about two.<br /> <br /> Now, if we work on average probability every two years we can assume<br /> Two homid kinfolk<br /> Two metis<br /> One lupus garou and 11 lupus kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <br /> If we take ten years we've got<br /> one or two homid garou and ten kinfolk<br /> Twenty metis. Four of them at first change or claith<br /> six lupus, five at first change or claith, 55 kinfolk.<br /> <br /> I'm being very lazy with the maths here. Just going to point that out so that nobody will feel entitled when they correct me on specifics.<br /> <br /> Now, That there collection of stats is under the assumption that we've got one mother doing all the work (and we're not taking into account fertility charms to raise litter sizes and assuming that the metis mother lives because precautions are taken) and it-doesn't-matter amounts of male involvement. I confess, I don't know the gender devide between wolves, but if we assume it's half, we've got twenty two kinfolk that are female, and if we assume they can breed after two years, we've got about 17 who can be pregnant and 12 who have given birth (I'm really, really not trying with these maths, but I don't think my accuracy hurts my validity) then we have 72 more wolves and 7 more lupus garou born in the final year alone. If we factor in the previous eight years that the original broodmother has been a grandmother for, we've got over the 20 garou of the metis broodmother. The one or two garou of the homids haven't changed yet (most likely, puberty can start at 9) and the kinfolk aren't at reproduction stages yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, this explosion in population might cause a wolf cull. Now, Warp what the black furies do- Kill the lupus males who don't change. Yeah it's brutal but<br /> -no wolf cull<br /> -Less chance of a non-garou parent mean more garou.<br /> -Less mouths to feed.<br /> <br /> Also, The black spirals (or glass walkers) could just do this from captivity.<br /> Now, other factors include that a lot of cubs don't reach maturity. Yeah, If garou cared for their cubs, it wouldn't be a problem. Hunting to feed a pack isn't so much of an issue for garou.<br /> <br /> Also, this has a good impact on actual animal populations. Khans for example. Amur tigers have liters of around 3-4 children a little over 3 months (with 5 month breaks). That's 5-6 children a year. Tigers are endangered. They wouldn't be if Khans bred more. More Khan, More tiger. A nice thing about this is that a feline female doesn't even need to search for a rare kinfolk tiger, she can just use a human father each time.<br /> <br /> Metis, really, for garou and bastet, are a waste for lupus mothers, unless of course they can create them out of season, in which case 3 months of a litter, 6 months of a metis and 3 months of a break would work wonders for the population.<br /> <br /> <br /> (as a side note, I'm surprised that the black furies don't have homids as a tiny minority or at least largely of adoption. wolf females are the only way such a tribe can sustain itself.)<br /> (Ratkin are clearly gaia's future, all hail our rodent overlords)<br /> *DEATH RAY*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 03-28-2016, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:50:01-07:00","id":854753,"title":"","content":"The garou hope to have a future after the final battle too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:47:28-07:00","id":854790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong#post854749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the garou are loosing lots of numbers, and the wolf population is low. The apocalypse is coming, the black spirals breed metis after metis for their front line infantry... Isn't this wrong? No, I don't mean 'wrong' as in 'oh no, world of darkness, you're being so horrible' I mean &quot;this isn't really the logical method&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>BSDs aren't particularly stable or sensible. It probably isn't a good idea to copy them; in fact, doing things similarly to the way they do them is probably a good sign that things have gone to pot and you should probably stop doing something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now this is more more or less true for changing breeds, because the pregnancy ranges from ten babies per week to one in a thousand years and all the parents will die, and maybe this is just my weaver tainted mind looking for effeciency where it would offend, but my argument: The animal breed should be the most populous. </div> </div> </div>Breeding is never efficient. It's a messy business that involves cultural invasiveness of the body, which is a terribly complex system still left with a vast amount of unknowns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's assume it takes a year or two to train cubs.<br /> <br /> You make one human every nine months<br /> OR<br /> One metis every six months<br /> OR<br /> You make aproximately six lupus (As much as 12) over three months, but can only do this once a year. </div> </div> </div>For changers that have litters, you generally get one shot for a changer per litter, not member of a litter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans will take... let's assume they change at 14.<br /> Metis take about 8<br /> Lupus take about two.<br /> <br /> Now, if we work on average probability every two years we can assume<br /> Two homid kinfolk<br /> Two metis<br /> One lupus garou and 11 lupus kinfolk. </div> </div> </div>11 lupus kin are going to be rare, even with Werewolf having more wolves alive than in real life (secret packs in places where they're extinct IRL, such as in Japan).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we take ten years we've got<br /> one or two homid garou and ten kinfolk<br /> Twenty metis. Four of them at first change or claith<br /> six lupus, five at first change or claith, 55 kinfolk.<br /> <br /> I'm being very lazy with the maths here. Just going to point that out so that nobody will feel entitled when they correct me on specifics.<br /> <br /> Now, That there collection of stats is under the assumption that we've got one mother doing all the work (and we're not taking into account fertility charms to raise litter sizes and assuming that the metis mother lives because precautions are taken) and it-doesn't-matter amounts of male involvement. I confess, I don't know the gender devide between wolves, but if we assume it's half, we've got twenty two kinfolk that are female, and if we assume they can breed after two years, we've got about 17 who can be pregnant and 12 who have given birth (I'm really, really not trying with these maths, but I don't think my accuracy hurts my validity) then we have 72 more wolves and 7 more lupus garou born in the final year alone. If we factor in the previous eight years that the original broodmother has been a grandmother for, we've got over the 20 garou of the metis broodmother. The one or two garou of the homids haven't changed yet (most likely, puberty can start at 9) and the kinfolk aren't at reproduction stages yet. </div> </div> </div>That could be seen as a likely maximum. You probably won't see anything close to it, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, this explosion in population might cause a wolf cull. Now, Warp what the black furies do- Kill the lupus males who don't change. Yeah it's brutal but </div> </div> </div>Black Furies killing male cubs? That sounds like something dumb from first edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, The black spirals (or glass walkers) could just do this from captivity. </div> </div> </div>Again, if your game plan starts resembling the one that the BSDs are using, back away and change it with all speed. You have gone astray.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, other factors include that a lot of cubs don't reach maturity. Yeah, If garou cared for their cubs, it wouldn't be a problem. Hunting to feed a pack isn't so much of an issue for garou.<br /> <br /> Also, this has a good impact on actual animal populations. Khans for example. Amur tigers have liters of around 3-4 children a little over 3 months (with 5 month breaks). That's 5-6 children a year. Tigers are endangered. They wouldn't be if Khans bred more. More Khan, More tiger. A nice thing about this is that a feline female doesn't even need to search for a rare kinfolk tiger, she can just use a human father each time. </div> </div> </div>A lot of beast born changers are probably going to be revolted by that prospect. You can't count on someone being happy playing the Crane Wife.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Metis, really, for garou and bastet, are a waste for lupus mothers, unless of course they can create them out of season, in which case 3 months of a litter, 6 months of a metis and 3 months of a break would work wonders for the population. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that having them can get you killed or exiled (and likely killed as a result of being ronin). It's literally the first rule of the Garou's list of Commandments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (as a side note, I'm surprised that the black furies don't have homids as a tiny minority or at least largely of adoption. wolf females are the only way such a tribe can sustain itself.) </div> </div> </div>Wow. You realize that all tribes other than the Red Talons are mostly Homid, right? And that even with generous secret packs, there aren't enough wolves in the world to compare to the weight of a fraction of seven billion humans?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Ratkin are clearly gaia's future, all hail our rodent overlords)<br /> *DEATH RAY* </div> </div> </div>They have the easiest time diverting resources from humans to live, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:50:12-07:00","id":854832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BSDs aren't particularly stable or sensible. It probably isn't a good idea to copy them; in fact, doing things similarly to the way they do them is probably a good sign that things have gone to pot and you should probably stop doing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>...but the wyrm is winning. <br /> Also, I'm not suggesting the garou copy them. Lupus, not metis. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breeding is never efficient. It's a messy business that involves cultural invasiveness of the body, which is a terribly complex system still left with a vast amount of unknowns.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're in a world where fertility charms can literally work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For changers that have litters, you generally get one shot for a changer per litter, not member of a litter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11 lupus kin are going to be rare, even with Werewolf having more wolves alive than in real life (secret packs in places where they're extinct IRL, such as in Japan).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not going to argue with the japanese wolf, If the garou had tighter control over their wolf kin, lupus kin wouldn't be too much of a problem. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if your game plan starts resembling the one that the BSDs are using, back away and change it with all speed. You have gone astray.</div> </div> </div> </div>The black spirals use most garou tactics. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of beast born changers are probably going to be revolted by that prospect. You can't count on someone being happy playing the Crane Wife.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revolted? Yeah, a lot of them will be. But it's the future of their race, and there's honour and wisdom for taking on the roll. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854790#post854790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. You realize that all tribes other than the Red Talons are mostly Homid, right? And that even with generous secret packs, there aren't enough wolves in the world to compare to the weight of a fraction of seven billion humans?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>A few of the tribes have much better lupus populations. Stargazers are pretty good, and one of my players swears the silver fangs have a great lupus population thanks to their excellent control over their kin. The pure land tribes do well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T20:18:46-07:00","id":854851,"title":"","content":"There's one big thing this misses: why the Gnawers are the biggest Tribe.<br /> <br /> Since you're only looking at what a single mother can be expected to birth, you're skipping how easy it is for a male Garou that doesn't give a shit about Purebreed to have a dozen kids a year. Even if most of those kids are kinfolk, flooding a population with kinfolk means the number of Garou that are born will increase significantly.<br /> <br /> You can't pull this off this kind of exponential spreading of kinfolk status with wolves. Metis can't have kids.<br /> <br /> It might not be the perfect strategy for the End Times since it will take a few generations to really pay off, but a few Tribes have been sowing the oats for a lot longer than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T20:43:23-07:00","id":854855,"title":"","content":"And there's one big issue with that; Spraying your seed doesn't garantee that your child will come to the right side. The wyrm is strong in cities. \u200bIt's a lot safer to spread kinfolk status across all wolves. <br /> <br /> (also, gnawers are the largest tribe because they'll take anyone, even garou who don't give a shit about fighting the wyrm and are only really in the tribe because it means they aren't hunted as ronin. The logic helping that even if they don't fight,maybe their kids will helps somewhat, but really, it isn't about coming in as many women as you can) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T22:12:21-07:00","id":854878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854832#post854832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but the wyrm is winning.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the ends and means tend to go hand in hand. Shit will follow shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'm not suggesting the garou copy them. Lupus, not metis. </div> </div> </div>There just aren't enough wolves to make that work, and human fear ensures that actual recovery will be met with guns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're in a world where fertility charms can literally work. </div> </div> </div>And they don't do much. Like how they do nothing to alleviate the skeeviness of these plans, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Source? </div> </div> </div>Extrapolation from page 67 of Nagah, where each given clutch of vasuki has a 10% chance of getting one Nagah. Presumably keeps for others, since there aren't vast and huge numbers of lupus Garou siblings from the same litter running around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I'm not going to argue with the japanese wolf, If the garou had tighter control over their wolf kin, lupus kin wouldn't be too much of a problem. </div> </div> </div>You can only exert so much control before you start to run into some serious problems will necessary wild wolf behavior. &quot;A wolf caged too easily turns into a dog,&quot; per Guardians of the Caerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The black spirals use most garou tactics. </div> </div> </div>No, there's a distinct lack of scorched earth corruption, rape, torture, binding banes into living beings to make fomori shock troops, and yet more on the part of the Gaian Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revolted? Yeah, a lot of them will be. But it's the future of their race, and there's honour and wisdom for taking on the roll. </div> </div> </div>And also some serious questions about losing the beast, since things can get weird and you might end up like Rokea and have the beast-born giving birth to homids. How long do you think you can run this clever work around before the shortcut gets closed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A few of the tribes have much better lupus populations. Stargazers are pretty good, and one of my players swears the silver fangs have a great lupus population thanks to their excellent control over their kin. The pure land tribes do well. </div> </div> </div>Stargazers are cited as having very few lupus, in spite of valuing them, because of how heavily they emphasize activities very much at odds with how most lupus have grown up; they may value lupus members, but that doesn't mean they have many of them. Even those tribes that boast more lupus than the Glass Walkers and Hakken are still heavily weighted toward homids; you won't find anything close to balance among them. It's actually a rather important point in the game's back story, as one of the many ways in which the lot of the Garou has gone horribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-29-2016, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T23:28:48-07:00","id":854894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854855#post854855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's one big issue with that; Spraying your seed doesn't garantee that your child will come to the right side. The wyrm is strong in cities. \u200bIt's a lot safer to spread kinfolk status across all wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gnawers esp. have been doing this for a couple thousand years. They've got plenty of tools for keeping track of their kids. They're experts at using the underclasses of societies to their advantage. Fostern Gnawers can easily patrol neighborhoods to watch of kids that are born kin or Garou (depending a bit on edition on whether they can tell which). An Adren Gnawer can keep track of even larger areas.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is strong in cities, sure, but don't read too much into the majority Garou Nation myths about cities vs. the reality the game makes clear. Two full Gaian Tribes are oriented around cities, with a large number of others having a large cultural reason to maintain ties with communities even when they end up in cities.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the simple fact that lots of people don't live in cities proper vs. all of the suburbs, towns, and similar places around cities.<br /> <br /> Is it as &quot;safe&quot; as wolves? Maybe. Depends too much on the location to say definitively. But it doesn't matter. There's 7 billion humans that Garou have been interbreeding with for thousands of years to create stable homid kinfolk populations within those billions.<br /> <br /> If you want to be incredibly generous about both the number of wolves in reality based on species that are arguably wolves or not, and all the canines Garou are capable of breeding with, and include all of the &quot;hidden&quot; populations of wolves the Garou have stashed around the world, you'd still not get to a million of them. With ~10,000 humans to every wolf/etc., mass breeding with humans easily produces more kinfolk and more Garou than &quot;playing it safe&quot; with wolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also, gnawers are the largest tribe because they'll take anyone, even garou who don't give a shit about fighting the wyrm and are only really in the tribe because it means they aren't hunted as ronin. The logic helping that even if they don't fight,maybe their kids will helps somewhat, but really, it isn't about coming in as many women as you can) </div> </div> </div>Erm. The Gnawers don't take people that aren't going to pull their weight in the Tribe. Even if they're more liberal about what contributing means, they don't tolerate Ronin that don't want the Ronin tag. They can not want to deal with the Garou Nation's shit, but they have to be one of Rat's children and deal with Rat's shit.<br /> <br /> And yes, taking in Garou (esp. Metis) other Tribes don't also inflates their numbers, but the &quot;breed with lots of humans&quot; method is definitely part of how they're as big as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T00:02:01-07:00","id":854900,"title":"","content":"There's truly a massive camp of bonegnawers that are basically just there so they don't have the ronin tag, and rat's seriously fine with this. Rat cares about survival, and having huge numbers is good for that; Eventually, the ones that don't fight will, and in the meantime they can make more children for his tribe. <br /> Source: the revised bone gnawers book. <br /> <br /> Also, Glass walkers. &quot;Gaian&quot;. Ha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:08:12-07:00","id":854914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854900#post854900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's truly a massive camp of bonegnawers that are basically just there so they don't have the ronin tag, and rat's seriously fine with this. Rat cares about survival, and having huge numbers is good for that; Eventually, the ones that don't fight will, and in the meantime they can make more children for his tribe.<br /> Source: the revised bone gnawers book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the rabble fall in and listen to the Grandparents, Aunts and Uncles when teeth need to get kicked in. These Garou aren't as dutiful or dedicated as the zealots of the other tribes, but they are still fighters in Gaia's war, when push comes to a very hard shove.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854900#post854900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Glass walkers. &quot;Gaian&quot;. Ha.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like saying the Uktena are of the Wyrm; some misguided characters within the setting may have thought as much, but that doesn't mean it is correct. The Glasswalkers <i>are </i>Gaian. Cockroach might have served the Weaver once, but he is still on Mama's side, just as he has been for eons.<br /> <br /> There are scenarios where the children of Cockroach fall to the Weaver. They ain't there yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:12:39-07:00","id":854916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854900#post854900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's truly a massive camp of bonegnawers that are basically just there so they don't have the ronin tag, and rat's seriously fine with this. Rat cares about survival, and having huge numbers is good for that; Eventually, the ones that don't fight will, and in the meantime they can make more children for his tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the camps count as this. The only camp even close are the Deserters, and they're one of the smallest Camps who still serve an important role as masters of the secret paths of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> If you mean the Rabble (not a camp), then you're severely misrepresenting them. The Rabble - as much as you can generalize about them - don't want to put up with Garou politics. Sure, most of them aren't die-hard warriors dedicating every day to kill Wyrm-spawn. But they're driven by the desire to do things their own way, not do nothing. And the book is fairly clear that the majority of the rabble come when called by the elders of the Tribe. That's what makes the Swarm so dangerous. To outsiders what looks like a handful of Gnawers can call on a dozen hanging around the edges of the local Protectorate to strike with numbers most Tribes can't come close to.<br /> <br /> There's a big difference between, &quot;left to their own devices until something big comes up,&quot; and, &quot;want to do nothing for the cause.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Source: the revised bone gnawers book. </div> </div> </div>It's generally good form to actually cite something if you're giving a source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Glass walkers. &quot;Gaian&quot;. Ha. </div> </div> </div>So, I'm just going to assume this nonsense means, &quot;Yes, you're right Heavy Arms, but I'm incapable of saying something like that, so I have to try to use being condescending with zero content to cover it up.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:16:11-07:00","id":854918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854900#post854900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, Glass walkers. &quot;Gaian&quot;. Ha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glass WAlkers might seem like technomancers only from the surface. But they represent humanity as a whole. And humanity is more than technology. It is keeping gardens and letting the parks grow. It is organized crime. It is free thinking and asking if old traditions have a point. I firmly believe there are small town GWs who represent mayors or new money rich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:21:37-07:00","id":854921,"title":"","content":"I imagine rat would want one of his children to contribute to the whole a little more then just producing more mouths to feed. After all a bum rat (pun intended) threatens the survival of all the other rats.<br /> <br /> You know I just had the thought about how Trailer Park Boys is an excellent example of bonegnawer kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons! 03-29-2016, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:22:20-07:00","id":854922,"title":"","content":"Not the wolf rape camps again... Seriously... The Lupus would never consider such a thing as it's compeltley against every instinct they have in their bones, and the humans who would find the whole thing palatable would pretty much be so insane that they'd probably be doing the Wyrm's work for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:04:37-07:00","id":854937,"title":"","content":"Rabble- Not a camp? Alright. Sure. Still, it's a 'group' and that 'really hard shove' has to be a really hard shove.<br /> <br /> Glass walkers- It was a joke.<br /> <br /> <br /> Asmodai, Not so much a rape camp as it is a really carefully monitored maintained wolf territory. Furthermore, Lupus are only burdened by child for 3 months, and have one season for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 03-29-2016, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:29:54-07:00","id":855086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854937#post854937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Asmodai, Not so much a rape camp as it is a really carefully monitored maintained wolf territory. Furthermore, Lupus are only burdened by child for 3 months, and have one season for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a puppy mill.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T11:43:48-07:00","id":855152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=854937#post854937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rabble- Not a camp? Alright. Sure. Still, it's a 'group' and that 'really hard shove' has to be a really hard shove.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Camp&quot; has a specific definition for the game. The Rabble is a general term for the majority of the Tribe that exists on the fringes of Garou society rather than actively engaging in Garou politics like the Rat's Teeth do. The Camps are societies within a Tribe, and pretty much only the Rat's Teeth are engaged enough to organize such things (and there's a nice list of them under &quot;camps&quot; in a few books that's pretty consistent).<br /> <br /> And it doesn't matter if it's a hard shove. The point is that they're not Ronin. They're just not falling in line with the mainstream Garou Nation. The Gnawer's acceptance of the Rabble might keep a lot of them from going full Ronin, but the whole point is that the Gnawers offer Garou that don't fit in with the traditional notions of the Nation a place within it instead of leaving them out in the cold like the other Tribes.<br /> <br /> Calling the Rabble Ronin-in-all-but-name is completely misrepresenting them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was a joke. </div> </div> </div>Why does that make it better?<br /> <br /> If you say something that's meant to be silly/funny/etc. and it bombs? It doesn't matter if it was a joke. If a comedian tells a joke to an audience and nobody laughs... is the comedian going to get anywhere by reminding everyone that they're telling jokes? Nope. Everyone already knew that.. and still didn't care about the joke part of it (or worse reacted poorly because it was a joke).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Asmodai, Not so much a rape camp as it is a really carefully monitored maintained wolf territory. Furthermore, Lupus are only burdened by child for 3 months, and have one season for it. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;rape camp&quot; thing is a factor in the logical conclusion of actually making an active lupus breeding program work.<br /> <br /> A Lupus might only be pregnant for 3 months, but the pups need raising.<br /> <br /> As well if you only rely on natural wolf breeding patterns, not only do they only breed once a year, but they only breed one female per pack. Going with my insanely inflated estimation of 700,000 wolves in the WoD, wolves generally have even numbers of both sexes, and average packs are ~7 wolves, you get down to only ~15,000 female wolves reproducing each year out of that 700,000 global population (and that quickly gets to ~1,000 per Tribe on average including the BSDs).<br /> <br /> &quot;Carefully monitored maintained wolf territory,&quot; isn't going to lead to the wolf-kin popping out an army of Lupus wolves. with so few of the females breeding. That means the non-mating females need to be forced into going against their instincts to breed. Which is how we get to the, &quot;oh no, not again,&quot; issue of hyperbolic stated rape-camps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:28:52-07:00","id":855219,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind is that Garou society is extremely conservative an devoted to their values which include dedication to nature and the natural. I would imagine that the great majority of Garou, especially those with the most access to wolf kinfolk, would find the idea of these sorts of tactics abhorrent. That doesn't mean that these sorts of methods wouldn't be effective, but I think that only a few Gaian werewolves would be willing to do this and those who would want to are going to catch a lot of flack from more conservative Garou.<br /> <br /> I think that the Black Spiral Dancers would do this, they probably do, which may be why the BSD's are winning. BSD's can use all sorts of breeding tactics that other Garou are going to object to - including treating kinfolk human women as harems, breeding wolf kinfolk in captivity, and even high-tech solutions like artificial insemination. With a bit of funding from Pentex, BSD's could probably set up a wolf breeding facility that could churn out huge numbers of wolf BSD kinfolk and new BSD lupus Garou. I see no reason why BSD's wouldn't do this or any number of other tactics to increase their numbers.<br /> <br /> I don't know if Glass Walkers would want to breed wolf kinfolk in captivity, I think that they would likely feel uncomfortable with that and even if they didn't, they would piss off the Garou Tribes who actually have the wolf kinfolk and so it wold lead to strife within the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting post though and I think it has given me some inspiration for Black Spiral Dancer activity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:13:09-07:00","id":855232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855219#post855219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind is that Garou society is extremely conservative an devoted to their values which include dedication to nature and the natural. I would imagine that the great majority of Garou, especially those with the most access to wolf kinfolk, would find the idea of these sorts of tactics abhorrent. That doesn't mean that these sorts of methods wouldn't be effective, but I think that only a few Gaian werewolves would be willing to do this and those who would want to are going to catch a lot of flack from more conservative Garou.<br /> <br /> I think that the Black Spiral Dancers would do this, they probably do, which may be why the BSD's are winning. BSD's can use all sorts of breeding tactics that other Garou are going to object to - including treating kinfolk human women as harems, breeding wolf kinfolk in captivity, and even high-tech solutions like artificial insemination. With a bit of funding from Pentex, BSD's could probably set up a wolf breeding facility that could churn out huge numbers of wolf BSD kinfolk and new BSD lupus Garou. I see no reason why BSD's wouldn't do this or any number of other tactics to increase their numbers.<br /> <br /> I don't know if Glass Walkers would want to breed wolf kinfolk in captivity, I think that they would likely feel uncomfortable with that and even if they didn't, they would piss off the Garou Tribes who actually have the wolf kinfolk and so it wold lead to strife within the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting post though and I think it has given me some inspiration for Black Spiral Dancer activity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are more reasons the Gaians do not to do this beyond 'the Garou Nation is conservative.' It devalues the wolf kinfolk, treats them like resources or commodities or even (in the worst cases) sex slaves. Wolves aren't just dumb animals in the WoD, they are quite intelligent. These plans would involve suffering, and lots of it... imagine the deleterious effects such programs would have on the spirit-world.<br /> <br /> Letting the world end in cataclysm is a superior alternative to the Garou enacting the forced breeding plots proposed above... I think we can all agree Innocent Flower is of the Wyrm, <i>nome de guerre</i> notwithstanding, trying to sell us an inherently tainted idea. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:15:05-07:00","id":855283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855232#post855232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there are more reasons the Gaians do not to do this beyond 'the Garou Nation is conservative.' It devalues the wolf kinfolk, treats them like resources or commodities or even (in the worst cases) sex slaves. Wolves aren't just dumb animals in the WoD, they are quite intelligent. These plans would involve suffering, and lots of it... imagine the deleterious effects such programs would have on the spirit-world.<br /> <br /> Letting the world end in cataclysm is a superior alternative to the Garou enacting the forced breeding plots proposed above... I think we can all agree Innocent Flower is of the Wyrm, <i>nome de guerre</i> notwithstanding, trying to sell us an inherently tainted idea. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not<i> just</i> conservatism, but some Gaian Garou do horrible things pretty frequently, so I don't just think it's a matter of being compassionate. I think that culling the human population or trying to wipe out the other Fera are both a lot worse than breeding wolves, but the Garou did do that stuff on a large scale. Granted, it has been a while. I get the impression that quite a few human kinfolk are treated so well also.<br /> <br /> I do think that Innocent Flower's suggestion works well for BSD's though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:46:56-07:00","id":855335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855219#post855219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind is that Garou society is extremely conservative an devoted to their values which include dedication to nature and the natural. I would imagine that the great majority of Garou, especially those with the most access to wolf kinfolk, would find the idea of these sorts of tactics abhorrent. That doesn't mean that these sorts of methods wouldn't be effective, but I think that only a few Gaian werewolves would be willing to do this and those who would want to are going to catch a lot of flack from more conservative Garou.<br /> <br /> I think that the Black Spiral Dancers would do this, they probably do, which may be why the BSD's are winning. BSD's can use all sorts of breeding tactics that other Garou are going to object to - including treating kinfolk human women as harems, breeding wolf kinfolk in captivity, and even high-tech solutions like artificial insemination. With a bit of funding from Pentex...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pet peeve: Pentex and its subsidiaries aren't the Bad Faction Piggybank. They deal with BSDs on a case by case basis, hiring &quot;consultants&quot; from among the fallen tribe but not really forming strong connections with very many of them. Francesco is a bit of an odd werewolf out when it comes to being where he is, doubly so for being a lupus BSD. Pentex has plenty of its own projects to furtively fund, like Mockery Breeds, fomori production, its post-apocalyptic game-plans to turn the world into a bunch of corporate fiefdoms, and useless initiatives that sound nice to employees but go nowhere and end up as empty and hollow words on excessively-produced hardcopy memoranda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:21:02-07:00","id":855363,"title":"","content":"Pentex would prefer not to relly on black spirals. They're useful tools, but they shouldn't be equals and are just as much rivals as they are allies.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaian breeding program. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Every year Male garou, regardless of breed, are encouraged to find wolves to carry their children.<br /> Garou are also encouraged to take time off and look after their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> The garou might need to take efforts to ensure that humans don't take notice of their lupus kin, policing their kinfolk. They might even need to reduce some of their own number selectively so that humans don't decide to do so outside of garou control.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it could be helped too if<br /> -The Dingo population was taken in. As I understand it, purely wild dingo can have children who breed true. The problem lies in that european domestic stock has diluted the dingo breed. Kill that stock to keep the dingo pure (yep, wolves wage war on the dogs. It's for nature) . This might actually result in a new Australasian tribe.<br /> -The rite that allowed garou to join with the african hunting dog could in turn be used on groups such as Ethiopian wolves, eastern wolves, red wolves or that legendary group of japanese wolves.<br /> <br /> Truly it sounds crazy but you could help a fair bit by just 'killing dogs'. Humans have done quite the bit of damage to nature with their dog breeding programs (IE bulldogs are a biological mess, despite being the cutest bludgers in nature). Dogs have a place In gaia's earth, but also cause a lot of damage, and are themselves damaged by human interference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Absolutely most evil Idea I've had which could possibly work for a story</b><br /> -A single Gaian garou or pack make use of captive female spiral dancers in order to mass produce gaian metis for the war effort. Obviously, the gaian garou aren't going to find out about this, and someone warped is doing this 'with the best of intentions':<br /> <br /> &quot;They are beyond redemption, their souls are for the wyrm. The only way they can be put to good use is to create for us, redeming the horrors it's caused with the gift of life.&quot;<br /> It's total psycho stuff. Chance might be that the villain in question might be touched by the wyld or even tainted by the wyrm for this kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Evil Idea</b><br /> A pack of gaian garou are hunting down ronin and spiral alike for use in turning their loyal kinfolk into gaian skindancers.<br /> <br /> I think both ideas are good in that they're sick, but ultimately 'for the greater good', and the players have a dillema in which their target is doing unlawful,vile, evil shit, but it's genuinely for a good, gaian cause. Each spiral defeated putting the garou one step closer to another comrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 03-29-2016, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:28:37-07:00","id":855376,"title":"","content":"Yeah because becoming as bad or worse then the followers of the wyrm to beat it is always an acceptable solution......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T18:24:29-07:00","id":855404,"title":"","content":"Capturing BSD females to rape them and keep them captive until they have Metis babies? I think there are a few flaws in that plan to say the least...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:10:20-07:00","id":855427,"title":"","content":"Also, you know, repeatedly (esp. systematically) violating the Litany on purpose is the kind of things lots of Garou will flat out kill you for. There isn't much fodder for player-character moral dilemmas to face the choice of just killing BSDs, or doing things a Philodox should have you sent to Erebus for just to make some Metis shock troops.<br /> <br /> If you want to play around with the morality of making shock troops... you'll get a ton more mileage out of things like presenting the PCs the option to create Gorgons in a semi-reliable fashion to have their own equivalent to Fomori/Drones to add to the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:38:42-07:00","id":855438,"title":"","content":"I was just presenting those last two things as story options. IE the players pack gets sent to investigate an area that's been sending nearby septs an unusually large number of metis, the metis providing little comment on their past. One pack of three recently doubled in number, sporting some unusually old claith in their rank, meanwhile garou disapearances have been occuring. <br /> <br /> The apocaylpse is coming. Garou get desperate and this is the world of darkness. Sometimes honour and wisdom are cast aside for fear and survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:16:51-07:00","id":855496,"title":"","content":"And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855363#post855363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but it's genuinely for a good, gaian cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is where those ideas fail to accomplish that. It isn't genuinely for a good Gaian cause because one option is objective a systemic violation of Gaian law (and not just in some sort of grey area loop hole, it's a flagrant abandonment of a fundamental law of Gaian society combined with <i>rape</i> just to make it even more objectively wrong by the Gaian cause), and the second still has plenty of Litany issues as well as other cultural taboos to contend with.<br /> <br /> These aren't genuinely for a good Gaian cause. They're like trying to save democracy by establishing yourself as an absolute dictator for life. It's just not how working for a cause goes.<br /> <br /> And because of that, any moral dilemma is lost. It's just PCs investigating a Sept that might not have danced the Spiral, but is rapidly on its way to falling to the Wyrm in its own way.<br /> <br /> The books have plenty of examples of Septs that are hiding nasty secrets. Yes, it's the WoD and the Garou are desperate. But this has nothing to do with the original topic of breeding pattern effectiveness. It's just a more complex antagonist for the PCs to contend with than the &quot;kill it quickly!&quot; Wyrm-spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:18:45-07:00","id":855568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855438#post855438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The apocaylpse is coming. Garou get desperate and this is the world of darkness. Sometimes honour and wisdom are cast aside for fear and survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think this, then you really are not getting the Shifters. The reason why they are where they are is because they are their culture and they are their Faith. And they will go out fighting for the same ideals. The only questions is if they will manage to find it within themselves to collaborate with those who should be their friends, or if they will go off alone into the dark, dark night.<br /> <br /> The whole point is in the setting that if you do what is wrong, you are ultimately corrupted and turned into a mockery of yourself. You're essentially having Garou that rape other Garou, that rape other wolves, and that murder whole species of Gaia's own for fun and profit. For a society based on honor, wisdom and glory, you sure as hell aren't giving them much of any of those.<br /> <br /> Just look at what the Cyberwolves did and what was their punishment, and what they did was way less of an intrusion then what you are suggesting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:22:24-07:00","id":855649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855232#post855232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Letting the world end in cataclysm is a superior alternative to the Garou enacting the forced breeding plots proposed above... I think we can all agree Innocent Flower is of the Wyrm, <i>nome de guerre</i> notwithstanding, trying to sell us an inherently tainted idea. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854749-aren-t-the-changing-breeds-doing-breeding-all-wrong?p=855363#post855363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Absolutely most evil Idea I've had which could possibly work for a story</b><br /> -A single Gaian garou or pack make use of captive female spiral dancers in order to mass produce gaian metis for the war effort. Obviously, the gaian garou aren't going to find out about this, and someone warped is doing this 'with the best of intentions':<br /> <br /> &quot;They are beyond redemption, their souls are for the wyrm. The only way they can be put to good use is to create for us, redeming the horrors it's caused with the gift of life.&quot;<br /> It's total psycho stuff. Chance might be that the villain in question might be touched by the wyld or even tainted by the wyrm for this kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Evil Idea</b><br /> A pack of gaian garou are hunting down ronin and spiral alike for use in turning their loyal kinfolk into gaian skindancers.<br /> <br /> I think both ideas are good in that they're sick, but ultimately 'for the greater good', and the players have a dillema in which their target is doing unlawful,vile, evil shit, but it's genuinely for a good, gaian cause. Each spiral defeated putting the garou one step closer to another comrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Confirmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}